- `--http-payload-size-limit` (default 100 MB, `crates/meilisearch/src/option.rs` line 99) bounds the number of body bytes. A stalled client never reaches the limit, so the limit never fires.
- actix-web's `client_request_timeout` (default 5 seconds) bounds reading the request head, not the body. Meilisearch does not set it, and it does not cover this read.
- `KeepAlive::Os` applies to idle keep-alive connections. A connection with a request in progress is not idle, so it is not reclaimed by keep-alive.
- The request task owns the socket descriptor and the temporary or update file. When the peer sends nothing, only the peer or process shutdown can release them.

