## Description

When the scheduler grants a permit to a waiting request in the
release path, it does not increment `searches_running`. The
immediate-admission path increments; the refill path does not.
Over time, `searches_running` falls below the real count.

## Root cause

The immediate-admission path at L154-156 increments before
granting:

```rust
if searches_running < usize::from(parallelism) && queue.is_empty() {
    searches_running += 1;
    let _ = search_request.send(Permit { sender: sender.clone() });
    continue;
}
```

The refill path at L146-152 decrements on release, then grants
a permit to the next waiter — but never increments:

```rust
searches_running = searches_running.saturating_sub(1);
if !queue.is_empty() {
    let remove = rng.gen_range(0..queue.len());
    let channel = queue.swap_remove(remove);
    let _ = channel.send(Permit { sender: sender.clone() });
}
```

After N refill grants, `searches_running` is N below the real count.

## Impact

`searches_running()` undercounts live searches. The admission gate
at L154 reads the wrong value and can let in more requests than
configured. Combined with the duplicate release signals from
`Permit::drop(self)` + `Drop for Permit` (#6578), the error grows:
two signals → two refill grants without increment → gate sees 0 →
admits yet another request.

## Expected behavior

Every grant must increment `searches_running` by 1:

```rust
searches_running = searches_running.saturating_sub(1);
if !queue.is_empty() {
    let remove = rng.gen_range(0..queue.len());
    let channel = queue.swap_remove(remove);
    let _ = channel.send(Permit { sender: sender.clone() });
    searches_running += 1;  // ← add this line
}
```

