    CreateMultipartUpload::parse_response(&body).map_err(|e| Error::S3XmlError(Box::new(e)))?;

let mut in_flight = VecDeque::<(JoinHandle<_>, Bytes)>::with_capacity(
    s3_max_in_flight_parts.get(),
);

for part_number in 1u16.. {
    if must_stop_processing.get() {
        return Err(Error::AbortedTask);
    }
    // ...
}
```

4. Each part request and its retry loop run in an independent Tokio task. The owner retains only a `JoinHandle` in `in_flight`:
   https://github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/blob/fff2ef5a42658b16a937d922aabc3fb7f89f2018/crates/index-scheduler/src/scheduler/enterprise_edition/s3.rs#L532-L558

```rust
let task = tokio::spawn({
    backoff::future::retry(retry_backoff.clone(), move || {
        let request = request.try_clone().unwrap();
        let request = request.send();
        async {
            match request.await {
                Ok(resp) if resp.status().is_client_error() => /* permanent error */,
                Ok(resp) => Ok(resp),
                Err(e) => Err(backoff::Error::transient(e)),
            }
        }
    })
});

in_flight.push_back((task, body));
```

Tokio documents that dropping a `JoinHandle` detaches the associated task; the task continues running and its return value is lost:
https://docs.rs/tokio/1.52.3/tokio/task/struct.JoinHandle.html

5. The visible terminal operation is success-side completion after all retained handles have been joined. There is no cancellation/error branch in this function that aborts child tasks and sends `AbortMultipartUpload`:
   https://github.com/meilisearch/meilisearch/blob/fff2ef5a42658b16a937d922aabc3fb7f89f2018/crates/index-scheduler/src/scheduler/enterprise_edition/s3.rs#L560-L600

```rust
for (handle, _buffer) in in_flight {
    let resp = join_and_map_error(handle).await?;
    extract_and_append_etag(&bump, &mut etags, resp.headers())?;
}

let action = bucket.complete_multipart_upload(
    Some(&credential),
    &object,
    multipart.upload_id(),
    etags.iter().map(AsRef::as_ref),
